      "text": "Step 4: Substitute \\( x = 2k \\) for the terms in the numerator and \\( x = 2k-1 \\) for the terms in the denominator:\n\\[ (2k)^4 + \\frac{1}{4} = \\left( (2k)^2 - 2k + \\frac{1}{2} \\right) \\left( (2k)^2 + 2k + \\frac{1}{2} \\right) = \\left( 4k^2 - 2k + \\frac{1}{2} \\right) \\left( 4k^2 + 2k + \\frac{1}{2} \\right), \\]\n\\[ (2k-1)^4 + \\frac{1}{4} = \\left( (2k-1)^2 - (2k-1) + \\frac{1}{2} \\right) \\left( (2k-1)^2 + (2k-1) + \\frac{1}{2} \\right) = \\left( 4k^2 - 6k + 2 + \\frac{1}{2} \\right) \\left( 4k^2 - 2k + \\frac{1}{2} \\right). \\]",
